Assignment 8: Pokemon!
This assignment added actual pokemon in their each of their uniqueness. First is the player can now choose a randomly generated starter pokemon when the program is first ran, this is chosen by pressing 1, 2, or 3. Random Trainers also have pokemon now, which are shown in the battle placeholder now. You can also see how many pokemon the trainer has and if they have more than 1 you can shuffle through them by pressing n/p, you still exit battles by pressing escape. Lastly, wild pokemon can be encountered in the tall grass (:), which similar to trainers you will be able to exit this placeholder by pressing escape. Shiny Pokemon, which are quite rare will be signified by their name being in yellow opposed to the typical white. I highly recommend running the program with the command "./main --numtrainers 2" just so it is easier to test the wild pokemon mechanic without constantly being stopped by trainers.

